<Wiki
  title="puv list"
  description="Show installed packages, extensions, and the dependencies of each."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>list</h1>
  <p>
    <code>puv list</code> prints what the project has installed: packages, extensions, and their
    dependencies.
  </p>

  <h2>The project graph</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv add symfony/console
puv add --dev phpunit/phpunit
puv list</pre>
  <p>
    After those two adds, the list includes <code>symfony/console</code>,
    <code>phpunit/phpunit</code>, their dependencies, and the extensions in that graph.
    Newer releases are a different command,
    <a href="/wiki/commands/audit"><code>puv audit</code></a>.
  </p>

  <h2>One package</h2>
  <p>
    The list is the whole graph. The reason a single name is present is
    <a href="/wiki/commands/why"><code>puv why</code></a>. Version, license, and authors for one
    release are <a href="/wiki/commands/info"><code>puv info</code></a>.
  </p>
  <pre class="block">puv why symfony/console
puv info symfony/console</pre>
</Wiki>
